  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A tall dressed stone, set upright at the head of a channel and cut with a single deep groove running the length of one face. The groove is the whole of the marking: the name is spoken, not written, and the stone says only that a name exists here and that a house holds it. It has been reset at least four times, on the evidence of four separate packing collars at the base, and each resetting followed the channel to a new position. It stands where it was last set and was recorded in place; what is in the collection is a cast, and the note that this is a cast has been lost from three separate publications.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
